# apps/web/.local.env - web env. One file per stage, same keys in each. Copy
# For credential-free verification use root `pnpm dev:local` / `pnpm build:local`.
# Those commands use wrangler.local.jsonc and ignore this file.
# this example to whichever you need:
#
#   .local.env   `pnpm dev` on your machine (stage `local`)
#   .dev.env     stage `dev`  - deployed on push to the `dev` branch.
#                Also reused as-is by PR preview stages (`pr-<N>`).
#   .prod.env    stage `prod` - deployed on push to the `main` branch.
#
# `.local.env` is needed BEFORE the first run:
#
#   cp apps/web/.local.env.example apps/web/.local.env
#
# `pnpm dev` passes `--env-file .local.env` and dies if the file is missing.
# An empty file is fine - nothing below is required for local development.
#
#   FOO=      fill this in
#   # FOO=    optional
#
# `.dev.env` / `.prod.env` are uploaded to GitHub Secrets by `pnpm sync:secrets`
# and written back by CI at deploy time. `.local.env` never leaves your machine.
#
# Control-plane credentials (CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN, ALCHEMY_STATE_TOKEN) live in
# `.alchemy.env` at the repo root, not here.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Custom domains
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Keep these in sync with `apps/server/.{stage}.env` - each app runs its own
# alchemy process with its own `--env-file` and reads only its own file.

# Frontend custom domain - the web Worker binds to it.
#
# Optional. PR previews always ignore it; the local stage hardcodes localhost.
# On dev/prod, unset means the auto-issued workers.dev URL.
# WEB_DOMAIN=app.example.com

# Backend custom domain - the web build uses it to work out the server URL
# baked into the browser bundle. Optional, same stage rules as WEB_DOMAIN.
# SERVER_DOMAIN=api.example.com

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Client-bundle env
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Add NEXT_PUBLIC_* keys here when you introduce browser-side configuration.
# Every one of them is inlined into the browser bundle at build time and is
# publicly readable - never put a secret behind this prefix.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SERVER_URL is deliberately absent: `alchemy.run.ts` assigns it
# unconditionally on every stage, so a value set here is silently discarded.
# See docs/deploy.md.
